<description>&lt;p&gt;Iraqi militias such as Kataib Hezbollah are publicly supporting the Houthis and urging Saudi Arabia to accept defeat, while Houthi rockets have struck Riyadh's King Khalid International Airport, prompting Iraqi condemnation. Iraqi air power has intensified, with fighter jets, F-16s and warplanes destroying Daesh and ISIS positions in eastern provinces and Diyala, including a recent hideout elimination. A major hospital fire in Baghdad forced over 60 evacuations, and a tire shop blaze added to civilian incidents in the capital. The TotalEnergies CEO visited Baghdad for oil and gas investment talks, and Iraqi authorities detained several Asian nationals and municipal staff at border and land sites. The conflict recorded 396 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxPV1l0MWlwOWZZVnFybnhpR1RjYllzZ3dBUXNLUWhvRzFNZUtDZkFoMUZYRmZqM016R2pHQThZMm84bFhCZEFITHlpelFuUFJ3a2dSTHZKcy1rYW53Nm03QTZUTlA5RXpGODlOeVYzaWhPdV9PZ3R5YW9ZWExydWEtNVRONVFSME82MzQyRnZBUmZrakk2UHhF?oc=5&quot;&gt;Kurdistan24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiS0FVX3lxTE8wQkFPN2U5QWZDTHdueFZ1R0ctZ1RwOGozRnFGWWwyQTBBUDZueXNYallWUU10TDZtVGg0bGM2ZS12NGRjcmh5eE9Wdw?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New Region&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;TRT World&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirAFBVV95cUxNNVJOUmlMVTA5TjcxU2RQY2xBb1M1aFpXZTVCOExEeXd2bXI4UllENDIzNGdULVZlb05IaEJRVjVxeUJuNVRuOVZJZXAxX3RxV196SnROdzljQ091bzN4bU91OUZldjk5ZEpEWG9MMXl5Z3VwYTRFek9DUUd6bXQyaHg1RERIVndFdDRHQWNJNFA5U3BTUTNlMGYwbUVRVUI4Q2swbm5lajduczJz?oc=5&quot;&gt;IraqiNews&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimAFBVV95cUxQbHl0RW5VZUhaWndXbDNvN2t4SkpDRGpYVUdLRmU0eTRGTFNRQ20xd1kxbEZlWkJ1YklZWklBbEZFekN2ZC1wS